BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:IU beINvolved Student Orgs
CATEGORIES:GroupBusiness
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an engaging and thought-provoking evening with Apa
 rna Shewakramani\, best known as a standout voice from Indian Matchmaking
 . A former attorney turned bestselling author\, television personality\, 
 and speaker\, Aparna has become a powerful advocate for self-worth\, inde
 pendence\, and unapologetic authenticity in both personal and professiona
 l spaces.\nIn this candid conversation\, Aparna will share her journey fr
 om corporate law to global recognition\, reflecting on the complexities o
 f identity\, cultural expectations\, and navigating modern relationships 
 in a highly public spotlight. Her experience on reality television sparke
 d global conversations about gender roles\, societal pressure\, and what 
 it means to stay true to yourself in environments that often demand compr
 omise.\nBeyond her television presence\, Aparna is the author of She’s Un
 likeable: And Other Lies That Bring Women Down\, where she challenges tra
 ditional narratives around likability\, ambition\, and confidence. Throug
 h storytelling and personal insight\, she encourages individuals to redef
 ine success on their own terms and to embrace their voice without apology
 .\nThis event will feature a moderated discussion followed by an interact
 ive Q&A session\, giving attendees the opportunity to engage directly wit
 h Aparna on topics such as career pivots\, navigating criticism\, buildin
 g confidence\, and redefining societal expectations. Whether you are inte
 rested in personal development\, media and culture\, or women’s empowerme
 nt\, this conversation offers valuable insights and meaningful takeaways.
 \nCome ready to challenge assumptions\, reflect on your own journey\, and
  be inspired to lead with confidence and authenticity.\n\n \n\nHosted by:
